Create a high-resolution black-and-white railroad operations form styled like modern CSX/NS dispatcher paperwork. The document should be formatted as a portrait 5x8 inch printable card with clean industrial typography, bold section headers, thin form borders, structured boxes, ruled handwriting areas, and grayscale shading suitable for black-and-white laser printing.

Use a professional railroad paperwork aesthetic — not a generic office form. The design should resemble authentic railroad job briefing forms, switch lists, or dispatcher-issued work cards.

Include:

* Small railroad logo in the upper-left corner in letterhead style
* Large railroad/company name header
* Division subtitle below the header
* Prominent boxed title section in upper-right corner
* Heavy outer border around entire card
* Internal boxed sections with consistent spacing and alignment
* Large lined “Instructions / Work Orders” area occupying roughly half the card
* Footer form number and revision information

Style requirements:

* Clean sans-serif typography
* Bold condensed headers
* Monochrome only
* High contrast
* Laser printer friendly
* No weathering or distressed textures
* Subtle gray header fills only
* Consistent border thickness
* Layout optimized for handwritten notes during operating sessions

The form should feel like authentic railroad operating paperwork used by crews, dispatchers, yardmasters, or industrial switching operations.

Keep the exact layout structure and styling consistent while allowing the text labels and fields to be modified for future variants.
